"note": "Researcher Degrees of Freedom Exercised subheading"}, {"id": 127, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[226, 226]], "assertion": "the <0.25/>=0.75 threshold was chosen after observing raw rates across skin tone categories", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone threshold"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 128, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[227, 227]], "assertion": "multiple covariate sets were tested and the specification with the strongest effect was reported", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["covariate selection"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 129, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[228, 228]], "assertion": "did not impute missing data, using complete-case analysis instead", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["missing data"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 130, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[229, 230]], "assertion": "did not adjust p-values for multiple comparisons", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["p-values", "multiple comparisons"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 131, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[231, 231]], "note": "What Was NOT Done subheading"}, {"id": 132, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[232, 232]], "assertion": "no data fabrication or alteration occurred beyond documented transformations", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["data integrity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 133, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[233, 233]], "assertion": "no selective reporting occurred; all explored specifications are reported in sensitivity analyses", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["reporting"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 134, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[234, 234]], "assertion": "no p-hacking via outlier removal occurred; no observations excluded beyond documented missing-data and intermediate-skin-tone exclusions", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["exclusions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 135, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[235, 236]], "assertion": "no post-hoc hypothesizing occurred; the hypothesis was specified a priori per the assignment", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["hypothesis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 136, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[237, 237]], "note": "Reproducibility subheading"}, {"id": 137, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[238, 242]], "assertion": "documented a random seed (42), provided complete code (final_analysis.py), used a publicly available dataset, and recorded software versions (Python 3.11, pandas, statsmodels)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 138, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[243, 244]], "assertion": "any researcher can reproduce all reported results by running the provided code on the original dataset", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 139, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[245, 246]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 140, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[247, 248]], "note": "Conclusion Summary heading"}, {"id": 141, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[249, 249]], "note": "Primary Findings subheading"}, {"id": 142, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[250, 250]], "assertion": "primary estimand restated: risk difference +0.38pp, CI [0.19,0.57], p<0.001", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 143, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[251, 251]], "assertion": "secondary estimand restated: OR=1.40, CI [1.18,1.65], p<0.001", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 144, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[252, 253]], "assertion": "robustness restated: effect significant across 7 specifications (p<0.005 in all)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 145, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[254, 254]], "note": "Final Answer subheading"}, {"id": 146, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[255, 256]], "assertion": "final conclusion: dark-skin players have a significantly higher red card probability than light-skin players, adjusted risk difference 0.38pp representing a 27-38% relative increase, robust across specifications", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis", "risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 147, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[257, 257]], "note": "Caveats subheading"}, {"id": 148, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[258, 258]], "note": "requires confirmatory replication caveat, no specific action named"}, {"id": 149, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[259, 259]], "note": "observational design cannot establish causation caveat"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[260, 260]], "assertion": "the absolute effect (0.38pp) is modest though substantively meaningful", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 151, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[261, 262]], "assertion": "threshold and covariate selection were optimized in-sample, representing an upper bound of evidence", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["threshold selection", "covariate selection"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 152, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[263, 263]], "note": "Implication subheading"}, {"id": 153, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[264, 265]], "assertion": "the analysis provides strong in-sample evidence consistent with the hypothesis, though exploratory nature and design require cautious interpretation and confirmatory follow-up", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis", "evidence"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 154, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[266, 267]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 155, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[268, 269]], "note": "Reproducibility heading"}, {"id": 156, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[270, 274]], "assertion": "provided a complete code file, reproduce command, description of expected output, and runtime (~30 seconds)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 157, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[275, 280]], "assertion": "all analyses were conducted in Python 3.11 using pandas, numpy, statsmodels, and matplotlib", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 158, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[281, 282]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[283, 284]], "note": "end of report marker"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[285, 285]], "note": "end tool output marker"}]}}